WEBVTT

00:16:28.524 --> 00:16:31.222
the effect was larger.

00:16:31.246 --> 00:16:32.398
Why?

00:16:32.422 --> 00:16:35.492
Because now the builders
loved it even more.

00:16:35.516 --> 00:16:36.722
(Laughter)

00:16:36.746 --> 00:16:38.902
They put all this extra effort into it.

00:16:39.352 --> 00:16:41.188
And evaluators?

00:16:41.212 --> 00:16:42.839
They loved it even less.

00:16:42.863 --> 00:16:46.712
Because in reality, it was even uglier
than the first version.

00:16:46.736 --> 00:16:48.077
(Laughter)

00:16:48.101 --> 00:16:52.073
Of course, this tells you something
about how we evaluate things.

00:16:52.835 --> 00:16:54.414
Now think about kids.

00:16:55.216 --> 00:16:58.323
Imagine I asked you, "How much
would you sell your kids for?"

00:16:59.748 --> 00:17:01.756
Your memories and associations and so on.